{{!
    The files waiting to be sent with the next chat message: one chip per file with its name, a
    thumbnail or a document icon, and a button that removes it.

    Rendered by aiinstructions.js into the attachment tray above the chat input.

    @template bookingextension_agent/attachment_tray

    @package    bookingextension_agent
    @copyright  2026 Wunderbyte GmbH <info@wunderbyte.at>
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Context variables required for this template:
    * attachments - List of waiting files, each with:
      * idx - Position in the list; the remove button carries it.
      * name - The file name shown to the user.
      * ispdf - Whether the document icon is shown when there is no thumbnail.
      * thumbnailhtml - The thumbnail as HTML from the upload web service, or empty.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "attachments": [
            {"idx": 0, "name": "handout.pdf", "ispdf": true, "thumbnailhtml": ""},
            {"idx": 1, "name": "photo.png", "ispdf": false, "thumbnailhtml": "<img class=\"booking-ai-thumb\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,AAAA\" alt=\"\">"}
        ]
    }
}}
{{#attachments}}<span class="booking-ai-attachment-chip" data-idx="{{idx}}">
    {{#thumbnailhtml}}{{{thumbnailhtml}}}{{/thumbnailhtml}}{{^thumbnailhtml}}{{#ispdf}}&#128196;{{/ispdf}}{{/thumbnailhtml}}
    <span class="booking-ai-attachment-name">{{name}}</span>
    <button type="button" class="booking-ai-attachment-remove" data-idx="{{idx}}" aria-label="{{#str}}ai_attachment_remove, bookingextension_agent{{/str}}" title="{{#str}}remove, moodle{{/str}}">&#10005;</button>
</span>{{/attachments}}
